{
  "info": {
    "_postman_id": "b8d4e2c0-5a17-4f6b-9c3e-1d7a0b4e8f25",
    "name": "Content Chain — Invitations pipeline",
    "description": "Smoke zaproszenia na **prawdziwy mail** (token z inboxa, nie z JSON i nie z cookies).\n\n**Dwa runy:** Setup → A. Create, potem wklej `inviteToken` z maila (`Token: …`), potem B. Accept.\n\nWymaga żywego `apps/api` (`:3001`), **istniejącego admina** (`adminEmail` / `adminPassword` jak w `auth.postman-collection.json`) oraz SMTP: `NODE_ENV=production` + prawdziwe `SMTP_*`. Przy `development` request create i tak da 201, ale mail **nie** wyjdzie (adapter logujący).\n\nUstaw `inviteEmail` lokalnie na swój adres — **nie** commituj go. Ten email jest jednorazowy: po accept (także po soft-delete) kolejny `POST /invitations` na ten sam adres → 409.\n\nCookie jar włączony domyślnie. W production cookies mają `Secure` — na `http://localhost` sprawdź po loginie Send → Cookies.\n\nTo nie jest `pnpm test:e2e` ani pełna suite `auth.postman-collection.json` (brak resend/revoke/bootstrap). Jak odpalić: `apps/api/test/postman/README.md`.",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
  "variable": [
    {
      "key": "baseUrl",
      "value": "http://localhost:3001/api/v1"
    },
    {
      "key": "originUrl",
      "value": "http://localhost:3001"
    },
    {
      "key": "adminEmail",
      "value": "admin@example.com"
    },
    {
      "key": "adminPassword",
      "value": "Password12!!"
    },
    {
      "key": "inviteEmail",
      "value": "your.email@example.com"
    },
    {
      "key": "invitePassword",
      "value": "Password12!!"
    },
    {
      "key": "inviteToken",
      "value": ""
    },
    {
      "key": "invitationId",
      "value": ""
    },
    {
      "key": "invitedUserId",
      "value": ""
    }
  ],
  "item": [
    {
      "name": "Setup",
      "description": "Login istniejącego admina. Konto nie jest tu tworzone — Bootstrap jest w `auth.postman-collection.json`. Przed A ustaw `inviteEmail` na adres, na który ma dojść mail.",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "POST login",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('status 200 (admin must already exist in DB)', function () {",
                  "  pm.response.to.have.status(200);",
                  "});",
                  "if (pm.response.code !== 200) {",
                  "  return;",
                  "}",
                  "const body = pm.response.json();",
                  "pm.test('admin session', function () {",
                  "  pm.expect(body.user.role).to.eql('admin');",
                  "  pm.expect(body.user.email).to.eql(pm.collectionVariables.get('adminEmail'));",
                  "});",
                  "pm.test('sets cc_access and cc_refresh cookies', function () {",
                  "  const cookies = pm.response.headers.all()",
                  "    .filter(function (h) { return h.key.toLowerCase() === 'set-cookie'; })",
                  "    .map(function (h) { return h.value; })",
                  "    .join('\\n');",
                  "  pm.expect(cookies).to.include('cc_access=');",
                  "  pm.expect(cookies).to.include('cc_refresh=');",
                  "});"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"email\": \"{{adminEmail}}\",\n  \"password\": \"{{adminPassword}}\"\n}\n"
            },
            "url": "{{baseUrl}}/auth/login",
            "description": "200 `{ expiresIn, user }` + cookies. 401 → brak admina albo inne hasło. Przy NODE_ENV=production i http://localhost: jeśli brak cookies, to flaga Secure — nie SMTP."
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "A. Create",
      "description": "Admin tworzy pending. Raw token **nie** jest w JSON — po 201 odbierz mail i wklej `inviteToken` (`Token: …`) zanim odpalisz B. Drugi POST na ten sam email → 409.",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "POST invitations unknown key (400)",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('status 400', function () {",
                  "  pm.response.to.have.status(400);",
                  "});",
                  "const body = pm.response.json();",
                  "pm.test('VALIDATION_FAILED unknown property', function () {",
                  "  pm.expect(body.code).to.eql('VALIDATION_FAILED');",
                  "  pm.expect(body.requestId).to.be.a('string').that.is.not.empty;",
                  "  pm.expect(body.details).to.be.an('array').that.is.not.empty;",
                  "});"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"email\": \"{{inviteEmail}}\",\n  \"password\": \"Password12!!\"\n}\n"
            },
            "url": "{{baseUrl}}/invitations",
            "description": "InviteUserDto = tylko email. Nieznany klucz → 400. Pending nie powstaje."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "POST invitations",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('inviteEmail is not the placeholder', function () {",
                  "  const email = pm.collectionVariables.get('inviteEmail');",
                  "  pm.expect(email, 'set inviteEmail to your real address').to.be.a('string').that.is.not.empty;",
                  "  pm.expect(email).to.not.eql('your.email@example.com');",
                  "});",
                  "pm.test('status 201', function () {",
                  "  pm.response.to.have.status(201);",
                  "});",
                  "if (pm.response.code !== 201) {",
                  "  return;",
                  "}",
                  "const body = pm.response.json();",
                  "pm.test('id email expiresAt without secrets', function () {",
                  "  pm.expect(body).to.include.keys('id', 'email', 'expiresAt');",
                  "  pm.expect(body.id).to.match(/^inv_/i);",
                  "  pm.expect(body.email).to.eql(pm.collectionVariables.get('inviteEmail'));",
                  "  pm.expect(body.expiresAt).to.be.a('string').that.is.not.empty;",
                  "  pm.expect(body).to.not.have.property('token');",
                  "  pm.expect(body).to.not.have.property('rawToken');",
                  "  pm.expect(body).to.not.have.property('tokenHash');",
                  "  pm.expect(body).to.not.have.property('accessToken');",
                  "  pm.expect(body).to.not.have.property('refreshToken');",
                  "});",
                  "pm.collectionVariables.set('invitationId', body.id);"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"email\": \"{{inviteEmail}}\"\n}\n"
            },
            "url": "{{baseUrl}}/invitations",
            "description": "201 `{ id, email, expiresAt }`. Token tylko w mailu (production SMTP) albo w logu (development). 409 gdy pending albo User na ten email już istnieje. 503 MAIL_DELIVERY_FAILED przy padzie SMTP po zapisie."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "POST invitations same email (409)",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('status 409', function () {",
                  "  pm.response.to.have.status(409);",
                  "});",
                  "const body = pm.response.json();",
                  "pm.test('CONFLICT pending invitation', function () {",
                  "  pm.expect(body.code).to.eql('CONFLICT');",
                  "  pm.expect(body.requestId).to.be.a('string').that.is.not.empty;",
                  "});"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"email\": \"{{inviteEmail}}\"\n}\n"
            },
            "url": "{{baseUrl}}/invitations",
            "description": "Drugi pending na ten sam email → 409 CONFLICT."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "GET invitations",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('status 200', function () {",
                  "  pm.response.to.have.status(200);",
                  "});",
                  "const body = pm.response.json();",
                  "const invitationId = pm.collectionVariables.get('invitationId');",
                  "pm.test('items include invitation without secrets', function () {",
                  "  pm.expect(body.items).to.be.an('array');",
                  "  const found = body.items.find(function (row) { return row.id === invitationId; });",
                  "  pm.expect(found).to.be.an('object');",
                  "  pm.expect(found).to.include.keys('id', 'email', 'createdAt', 'expiresAt', 'invitedBy');",
                  "  pm.expect(found.email).to.eql(pm.collectionVariables.get('inviteEmail'));",
                  "  pm.expect(found.invitedBy).to.include.keys('id', 'email');",
                  "  pm.expect(found.invitedBy.email).to.eql(pm.collectionVariables.get('adminEmail'));",
                  "  body.items.forEach(function (row) {",
                  "    pm.expect(row).to.not.have.property('token');",
                  "    pm.expect(row).to.not.have.property('rawToken');",
                  "    pm.expect(row).to.not.have.property('tokenHash');",
                  "  });",
                  "});"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": "{{baseUrl}}/invitations",
            "description": "Lista pending. Pola: id, email, createdAt, expiresAt, invitedBy. Bez hashu/tokenu."
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "B. Accept",
      "description": "Wymaga `inviteToken` wklejonego z maila po A (nie z cookies). Pierwszy request czyści cookie jar — accept jest publiczny, bez sesji admina. Potem login nowym kontem i 403 na zasoby admina. Pipeline **nie** soft-delete'uje konta.",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "POST accept-invite weak password (400)",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "prerequest",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "const origin = pm.collectionVariables.get('originUrl') || 'http://localhost:3001';",
                  "try {",
                  "  pm.cookies.jar().clear(origin, function () {});",
                  "} catch (e) {",
                  "  console.warn('cookie jar clear skipped', e);",
                  "}"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('inviteToken is set (paste Token from the invitation email)', function () {",
                  "  pm.expect(pm.collectionVariables.get('inviteToken'), 'inviteToken').to.be.a('string').that.is.not.empty;",
                  "});",
                  "pm.test('status 400', function () {",
                  "  pm.response.to.have.status(400);",
                  "});",
                  "const body = pm.response.json();",
                  "pm.test('VALIDATION_FAILED password policy', function () {",
                  "  pm.expect(body.code).to.eql('VALIDATION_FAILED');",
                  "});"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"token\": \"{{inviteToken}}\",\n  \"password\": \"short\"\n}\n"
            },
            "url": "{{baseUrl}}/auth/accept-invite",
            "description": "Ważny token + hasło poza A-5 → 400; pending bez zmian. Ten sam token działa w następnym requestcie."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "POST accept-invite",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "prerequest",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "const origin = pm.collectionVariables.get('originUrl') || 'http://localhost:3001';",
                  "try {",
                  "  pm.cookies.jar().clear(origin, function () {});",
                  "} catch (e) {",
                  "  console.warn('cookie jar clear skipped', e);",
                  "}"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('inviteToken is set (paste Token from the invitation email)', function () {",
                  "  pm.expect(pm.collectionVariables.get('inviteToken'), 'inviteToken').to.be.a('string').that.is.not.empty;",
                  "});",
                  "pm.test('status 201', function () {",
                  "  pm.response.to.have.status(201);",
                  "});",
                  "if (pm.response.code !== 201) {",
                  "  return;",
                  "}",
                  "const body = pm.response.json();",
                  "pm.test('user role user without tokens', function () {",
                  "  pm.expect(body).to.have.property('user');",
                  "  pm.expect(body.user).to.include.keys('id', 'email', 'role');",
                  "  pm.expect(body.user.id).to.match(/^usr_/i);",
                  "  pm.expect(body.user.email).to.eql(pm.collectionVariables.get('inviteEmail'));",
                  "  pm.expect(body.user.role).to.eql('user');",
                  "  pm.expect(body).to.not.have.property('accessToken');",
                  "  pm.expect(body).to.not.have.property('refreshToken');",
                  "  pm.expect(body.user).to.not.have.property('passwordHash');",
                  "});",
                  "pm.test('does not set cc_access or cc_refresh', function () {",
                  "  const cookies = pm.response.headers.all()",
                  "    .filter(function (h) { return h.key.toLowerCase() === 'set-cookie'; })",
                  "    .map(function (h) { return h.value; })",
                  "    .join('\\n');",
                  "  pm.expect(cookies).to.not.include('cc_access=');",
                  "  pm.expect(cookies).to.not.include('cc_refresh=');",
                  "});",
                  "pm.collectionVariables.set('invitedUserId', body.user.id);"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"token\": \"{{inviteToken}}\",\n  \"password\": \"{{invitePassword}}\"\n}\n"
            },
            "url": "{{baseUrl}}/auth/accept-invite",
            "description": "Publiczny. 201 `{ user }` z role=user. Bez Set-Cookie. Potem zwykły login."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "POST accept-invite reused token (401)",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "prerequest",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "const origin = pm.collectionVariables.get('originUrl') || 'http://localhost:3001';",
                  "try {",
                  "  pm.cookies.jar().clear(origin, function () {});",
                  "} catch (e) {",
                  "  console.warn('cookie jar clear skipped', e);",
                  "}"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('status 401', function () {",
                  "  pm.response.to.have.status(401);",
                  "});",
                  "const body = pm.response.json();",
                  "pm.test('UNAUTHORIZED used token', function () {",
                  "  pm.expect(body.code).to.eql('UNAUTHORIZED');",
                  "  pm.expect(body.message).to.eql('Invalid invitation token');",
                  "});"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"token\": \"{{inviteToken}}\",\n  \"password\": \"{{invitePassword}}\"\n}\n"
            },
            "url": "{{baseUrl}}/auth/accept-invite",
            "description": "Zużyty token → 401 (ten sam komunikat co zły token)."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "POST login as invited user",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('status 200', function () {",
                  "  pm.response.to.have.status(200);",
                  "});",
                  "const body = pm.response.json();",
                  "pm.test('user session without tokens in body', function () {",
                  "  pm.expect(body.user.email).to.eql(pm.collectionVariables.get('inviteEmail'));",
                  "  pm.expect(body.user.role).to.eql('user');",
                  "  pm.expect(body).to.not.have.property('accessToken');",
                  "});",
                  "pm.test('sets cc_access and cc_refresh cookies', function () {",
                  "  const cookies = pm.response.headers.all()",
                  "    .filter(function (h) { return h.key.toLowerCase() === 'set-cookie'; })",
                  "    .map(function (h) { return h.value; })",
                  "    .join('\\n');",
                  "  pm.expect(cookies).to.include('cc_access=');",
                  "  pm.expect(cookies).to.include('cc_refresh=');",
                  "});"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"email\": \"{{inviteEmail}}\",\n  \"password\": \"{{invitePassword}}\"\n}\n"
            },
            "url": "{{baseUrl}}/auth/login",
            "description": "Login nowym kontem po accept-invite → 200 + cookie."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "POST invitations as user (403)",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
